     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "'\\n## What is\\xa0CLIP?\\n**Contrastive\\xa0Language–Image\\xa0Pre‑Training (CLIP)** is a vision‑language model introduced by OpenAI in\\xa02021. It was trained on **400\\u202fM** image–text pairs scraped from the internet and learned to embed images and sentences in a shared vector space. Because of this alignment it can perform **zero‑shot classification**: we give it prompts such as \"a photo of an indoor scene\" vs. \"a photo of an outdoor scene\" and CLIP estimates which description better matches the image *without any additional training*.\\n'"
      ]
     },
